{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1793711200","published":"2026-11-03T13:06:52Z","modified":"2026-11-20T10:17:26.898372679Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-119373","CVE-2026-119375","CVE-2026-119378","CVE-2026-119379"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-119373, CVE-2026-119375, CVE-2026-119378, CVE-2026-119379","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow in the session extension\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-119379.patch: re-validate the table on every\n       table header in sqlite3changeset_apply() in\n       ext/session/sqlite3session.c, so a changeset that repeats a table\n       name with a larger column count is checked against the schema again\n     - CVE-2026-119379\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow in FTS5 detail=none prefix merge\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-119373.patch: account for negative rowids\n       when sizing the output buffer in fts5MergeRowidLists() in\n       ext/fts5/fts5_index.c\n     - CVE-2026-119373\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: use-after-free in the R-Tree extension\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-119378.patch: treat a zero\n       sqlite3_last_insert_rowid() after a node insert as corruption in\n       nodeWrite() in ext/rtree/rtree.c\n     - CVE-2026-119378\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: uninitialized memory read via undersized WAL page size\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-119375.patch: zero the part of the page\n       buffer not covered by the WAL frame in sqlite3WalReadFrame() in\n       src/wal.c\n     - CVE-2026-119375","affected":[{"package":{"name":"lemon","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:20.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/lemon?distro=ubuntu-20.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"3.31.1-4ubuntu0.7+tuxcare.els3"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu20.04els/CLSA-2026-1793711200.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libsqlite3-0","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:20.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libsqlite3-0?distro=ubuntu-20.04"},"ranges":[{"type